  "lapsed_date": "01/09/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed communal area would be too deep and served solely by a rear window and rooflights, providing no good quality outlook and light resulting in an inadequate level of shared amenity for a 7-person HMO. Further to this, the proposed ground floor arrangement would not result in a satisfactory layout by virtue of the lack of adequate functional communal space which would be disturbed by the passage of bicycles directly via the only communal space to be provided. Taken together, the scheme fails to provide an acceptable standard of living for future occupiers, contrary to Policies DMD 5 (Residential conversions) and DMD 8 (Houses in Multiple Occupation) of Enfield's Development Management Document (2014), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Chapter 12 of the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the siting of cycle parking within the rear garden and obstructed access route via the ground floor kitchen area, would fail to provide cycle parking provision in line with London Plan standards and would be prohibitive to the promotion of cycling as both a healthy and sustainable form of transport, contrary to Policies DMD 5, DMD 8 and DMD 47 of the Development Management Document (2014), Policies T2 and T5 of the London Plan (2021) and Core Policy 25 of Core Strategy (2010)."
  ],
